  "note": "Registers and warps per SM come from the nsys launch records, not a model: each population is split by register count because one short name covers four tracers here and only the Chen 2022 snow one is register-heavy. The treated saving is resolved against the untreated broadcasts of the same block (worst_control_delta_ms), which bound run-to-run noise at the same scale. It is NOT resolved in the arm total: untreated_drift_ms is the sum of every other kernel's change, and it is the larger number, which is why arm_total_resolved is false and no end-to-end claim is made here. end_to_end prices the same treatment on the unprofiled AMIP pair. It does not resolve: the margin over the floor between identical arms is a fraction of the spread between the nulls that set the floor, and max_points_if_fully_converted shows that even a perfect conversion of the device saving could not have cleared it. Read the per-kernel figures, not this one.",
